  "notes": "なくなる means to disappear, be gone, or run out.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: なくす (transitive - to lose)\n\nFORMATION:\nない (not exist) + なる (become) = なくなる\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- お{金|かね}がなくなる: money runs out\n- {時間|じかん}がなくなる: time runs out\n- {痛|いた}みがなくなる: pain disappears\n- {在庫|ざいこ}がなくなる: out of stock\n\nIMPORTANT DISTINCTION:\n- なくなる: to disappear, run out (things)\n- {亡|な}くなる: to pass away (euphemism for death)\n\nUSAGE NOTE:\n{亡|な}くなる is the polite way to say someone died, while {死|し}ぬ is more direct.",
